Original commit body from 1b478165c3f11a543b0e224a7c780851e846cc46:

linkers/type_hierarchy — the language-neutral linker that emits
interface-method -> impl-method dispatches_to for every language — split
qualified member names on '#' and '.' but NOT '::', so
_get_method_short_name("MyTrait::method") returned the whole string and
_get_class_name_from_method returned None. It was structurally incapable
of firing for Rust, which is why a Rust-specific dispatch linker exists
at all.

Rust now emits dispatches_to: Shape::area -> Square::area, matching every
other language. Its parity-column cell is promoted from strict-xfail hole
to hard pass in the same PR — the XPASS failed the run and forced it,
which is the whole point of the strict marker.

THE FACT NOW HAS ONE HOME, AND IT WAS RECORDED IN SIX PLACES.
hypergumbo_core.member_names owns MEMBER_NAME_SEPARATORS plus
split_member_name / member_owner / member_short_name. Swept:
containment, method_call_recovery, type_hierarchy, receiver_blind_magnets
(whose private copy was ordered ("::", "#", ".") — wrong, since Ruby's
Foo::Bar#baz splits at the '#'), and three route_handler sites that knew
only ("#", ".") and so could not index a Type::handler route. A live-tree
linter with a planted-offender test prevents a seventh copy.

NOT folded into qualified_name_axis: that maps a language to its
module-path separator (php -> backslash), this is the owner/member
separator in Symbol.name. They coincide for Rust and diverge for PHP,
whose members are dotted — folding would mis-split every PHP member. The
linter exempts literals containing a separator outside this vocabulary,
and exempts per-language analyzer packages.

rust_trait_dispatch NARROWED, NOT RETIRED, AND NO EDGE IS LOST. It fanned
dispatch from a trait to every method of implementing structs —
deliberate over-approximation, since the alternative was declaring ~3000
live functions dead. It now skips the trait-required methods the shared
linker covers precisely and keeps only the inherent ones. An EMPTY
requirement set means "cover everything", not "cover nothing": an
external trait, or an analyzer that failed to emit members, falls back to
the old behaviour. Measured on three fixtures — trait method precise,
inherent method retained, marker trait with zero requirements retained.

The ADR-0023 §3 allow-list entry from INV-fimon STAYS and is now
permanently legitimate: the (trait,rust)->(method,rust) partition still
carries contains + dispatches_to because inherent dispatch keeps the
trait anchor. The ADR's caveat that its removal was conditional is the
condition failing, as written.

